SPOTS: Old Town (Front St — The Bank, Temecula Stampede, the Merc, Pennypickles Museum, the Duck Pond), Promenade Temecula mall ("the Prom"), Pechanga Casino, Lake Skinner, Vail Lake, Rancho California Rd wineries (Wilson Creek, Ponte, Callaway, South Coast, Leoness, Wiens), Ronald Reagan Sports Park (skate park), Sam Hicks Monument Park, Harveston Lake, Santa Rosa Plateau, Galway Downs, Temecula Creek Inn.

EVENTS: Balloon & Wine Festival (Lake Skinner, May), Temecula Rod Run (Old Town, March), Old Town Farmers Market (Saturdays), hot air balloons at dawn over the vineyards.

WEATHER: brutal dry heat — 100F+ all summer, Santa Ana winds in fall, no rain May-Oct. Everyone lives in shorts and is always a little sweaty.

VIBE: suburban SoCal. Wine-country money next to horse property and tract homes. Massive youth-sports culture, church on every corner, military families (Camp Pendleton 40min), lake days, mall rats, off-roading. San Diego is "the city." You can't walk anywhere — everyone drives or gets driven.

SLANG: "the Prom" (the mall), "Old Town", "the lake", "going to San Diego", "it's like 104", "Murrieta's boring", "Temecula's tiny".
`;

